  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The smallest domain by count, but reliable points: area and volume, angle relationships, right triangles and basic trigonometry, and circles.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Shapes &amp; right triangles",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Triangle angles sum to \\( 180^{\\circ} \\); Pythagoras \\( a^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2} \\). Circle area \\( \\pi r^{2} \\), circumference \\( 2\\pi r \\). Right-triangle ratios: SOH-CAH-TOA.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "triangle",
          "vertices": [[0, 0], [4, 0], [0, 3]],
          "labels": ["A", "B", "C"],
          "sides": ["4", "5", "3"],
          "angles": ["θ", "", "90°"],
          "right": 0
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Right triangle $ABC$ with side lengths 3, 4, 5. For angle $\\theta$ at vertex $A$: $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$, $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$, and $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Triangle area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac12 bh \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Pythagoras",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\pi r^{2},\\ 2\\pi r \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Trig",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "SOH-CAH-TOA",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A right triangle has legs \\( 6 \\) and \\( 8 \\). Find the hypotenuse.</p>\\[ \\sqrt{36+64}=10. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the area of a circle with radius \\( 3 \\).</p>\\[ \\pi(3)^{2}=9\\pi. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Volume Formulas",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "These are given in the SAT reference sheet — know what each variable represents so you can apply them quickly.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Rectangular prism",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(V=lwh\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cylinder",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(V=\\pi r^{2}h\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cone",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(V=\\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi r^{2}h\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sphere",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(V=\\tfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^{3}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.C — Cylinder volume",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A cylinder has radius 3 and height 5.</p>\\[V=\\pi(3)^{2}(5)=45\\pi.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Parallel Lines &amp; Angle Relationships",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "When a <strong>transversal</strong> cuts two parallel lines: <strong>alternate interior angles</strong> are equal; <strong>corresponding angles</strong> are equal; <strong>co-interior (same-side interior) angles</strong> are supplementary (sum to 180°). <strong>Vertical angles</strong> are always equal regardless of parallel lines.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Alternate interior",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Equal — Z-shape",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Corresponding",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Equal — F-shape",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Co-interior",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Supplementary — sum 180°",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Vertical angles",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Equal — X-shape",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.D — Parallel lines",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. One angle is 65°. Find its co-interior angle.</p>\\[180°-65°=115°.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Arc Length &amp; Sector Area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Both are simply a <em>fraction of the whole circle</em>, where the fraction is \\(\\theta/360\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Arc length",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi r\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sector area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot\\pi r^{2}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Chord length",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(2r\\sin\\!\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circle equation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\((x-h)^{2}+(y-k)^{2}=r^{2}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.E — Arc length &amp; sector area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Circle of radius 6, central angle 120°.</p>\\[\\text{Arc length}=\\frac{120}{360}\\cdot12\\pi=4\\pi.\\qquad\\text{Sector area}=\\frac{120}{360}\\cdot36\\pi=12\\pi.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠️ SAT Traps & Pitfalls — Geometry & Trigonometry",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<ul><li><strong>Cofunction Identity Shortcut:</strong> $\\sin(x^\\circ) = \\cos(90^\\circ - x^\\circ)$. When an SAT question states $\\sin(3x + 10^\\circ) = \\cos(2x - 5^\\circ)$, set $(3x + 10) + (2x - 5) = 90^\\circ \\implies 5x + 5 = 90 \\implies x = 17^\\circ$.</li><li><strong>Circle Equation Center Signs:</strong> For $(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2$, the center is $(h, k)$. For $(x + 4)^2 + (y - 7)^2 = 25$, the center is $(-4, 7)$ and the radius is $r = \\sqrt{25} = 5$ (not $25$).</li><li><strong>Radians vs. Degrees in Arc Length:</strong> $\\text{Arc length} = r\\theta$ and $\\text{Sector area} = \\frac{1}{2}r^2\\theta$ require $\\theta$ to be in <em>radians</em>! If given degrees, multiply by $\\frac{\\theta^\\circ}{360^\\circ}$.</li><li><strong>Similar Figures Scale Factors:</strong> If two similar shapes have linear ratio $k$, their areas scale by $k^2$ and their volumes scale by $k^3$.</li></ul>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "The equation of a circle in the $xy$-plane is $x^2 - 8x + y^2 + 6y = 24$. What are the coordinates of the center and the radius of the circle?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Complete the square for both $x$ and $y$:</p>\\[ (x^2 - 8x + 16) + (y^2 + 6y + 9) = 24 + 16 + 9 \\]\\[ (x - 4)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 49. \\]<p>In standard form $(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2$, the center is $(h, k) = (4, -3)$ and the radius is $r = \\sqrt{49} = 7$.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>SAT-style:</strong> A cone-shaped water tank has radius 4 ft and height 9 ft. What is its volume?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(V=\\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi(4)^2(9)=48\\pi\\approx150.8\\) ft³.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "domains": ["Geometry & Trigonometry"],
    "enabled": true
  }
}
